    {
      "text": "take away thy coat, let him have thy cloak also, Matt. 5:40 (Luke 6:29; 3 Ne. 12:40). Himself took our infirmities, Matt. 8:17. he that taketh not his cross, and followeth after me, Matt. 10:38. Take my yoke upon you, Matt. 11:29. from him shall be taken away even that he hath, Matt. 13:12 (25:29; Mark 4:25; Luke 8:18; 19:26). let him … take up his cross, Matt. 16:24 (Mark 8:34; Luke 9:23). kingdom of God shall be taken from you, Matt. 21:43. one shall be taken, and the other left, Matt. 24:40 (Luke 17:34; JS—M 1:44). Take therefore the talent from him, Matt. 25:28. Take, eat; this is my body, Matt. 26:26 (Mark 14:22; 1 Cor. 11:24). take away this cup from me, Mark 14:36. take ye no thought how … ye shall answer, Luke 12:11. Take from him the pound, Luke 19:24. he took the cup … and said, Take this, and divide it, Luke 22:17. he took bread, and blessed it, Luke 24:30. Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world, John 1:29 (1 Ne. 10:10). I lay down my life, that I might take it again, John 10:17. not that thou shouldest take them out of the world, John 17:15. officers of the Jews took Jesus, John 18:12. while they beheld, he was taken up, Acts 1:9. take unto you the whole armour of God, Eph. 6:13 (D&C 27:15). ye shall take it patiently, 1 Pet. 2:20. hold that fast … that no man take thy crown, Rev. 3:11. let him take the water of life freely, Rev. 22:17. if any man shall take away from the words, Rev. 22:19.",
